From: AdrielOrihuela <adriel.orihuela.m@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 20:02:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Expose the hidden-entity half of canSee by id

The locator bar has to ask whether a player can see somebody being ticked
by another region thread. The other half of canSee travels in a snapshot,
so this half only needs the id, and asking by id touches nothing but the
asking player's own map.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftPlayer.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftPlayer.java
index 24f7cf40ffd6bbb154dc664bc9f7e6661247f2ac..e4bffe61ee47b9217d73d5339ad30904709b2f9f 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftPlayer.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftPlayer.java
@@ -2104,6 +2104,15 @@ public class CraftPlayer extends CraftHumanEntity implements Player, PluginMessa
         return this.equals(entity) || entity.isVisibleByDefault() ^ this.invertedVisibilityEntities.containsKey(entity.getUniqueId()); // SPIGOT-7312: Can always see self
     }
 
+    // LegacyFolia start - half of canSee, by id
+    // The locator bar has to answer canSee about somebody being ticked by another region thread.
+    // The other half of it, isVisibleByDefault, belongs to that entity and is carried across in a
+    // snapshot; this half is this player's own map, so asking by id touches nothing but us.
+    public boolean isHiddenEntity(final java.util.UUID uuid) {
+        return this.invertedVisibilityEntities.containsKey(uuid);
+    }
+    // LegacyFolia end - half of canSee, by id
+
     public boolean canSeePlayer(UUID uuid) {
         org.bukkit.entity.Entity entity = this.getServer().getPlayer(uuid);
 
